ue":124},"Connections",{"type":22,"value":126},"Updated",{"type":22,"value":128},"Need to know",{"type":22,"value":130},"Depends on",{"type":22,"value":132},"Used by",{"type":22,"value":134},"Externals",{"m":136},"function m(number, one, few, includeNumber = true) {\n  const text = number === 1 ? one : few;\n  return includeNumber ? `${number} ${text}` : text;\n}",{"contentPath":138,"mainContent":139},"group/foundations/equations/",{"fullId":140,"shortId":140,"contentRelativePath":141,"title":142,"bookTitle":15,"breadcrumbs":143,"description":146,"stats":147,"connections":153,"contributions":172,"type":177,"children":178},"foundations/equations","01-foundations/02-equations","Equations",[144],{"icon":145,"title":15,"link":17},"book-outline","\n    An overview of equations and equation solving: elementary equations,\n    quadratic equations, and systems of equations.\n    Learn why equations are solved and how they model real-world processes.\n    Includes transformations, domain restrictions, loss of solutions,\n    and extraneous roots.\n  ",{"materials":148,"elements":149},5,{"accent_term":150,"accent_statement":151,"accent_important":150,"problem":152},7,4,59,{"externals":154},[155,163],{"type":156,"items":157},"own",[158],{"type":159,"title":160,"info":161,"reason":162},"physical","Algebra Word Problems","Anita Harnadek","Huge collection of word problems which lead to an equations with detailed solutions.",{"type":164,"title":15,"items":165},"parent",[166],{"type":167,"title":168,"info":169,"link":170,"reason":171},"web","LibreTexts Mathematics","An open and free online collection of mathematics educational materials.","https://math.libretexts.org/","A large amount of materials and many typical practice problems.",[173],{"contributorId":174,"name":175,"avatarUrl":176},"gwynerva","Peter Radko","/file/contributors/gwynerva/avatar.png","group",[179,262,269],{"type":180,"link":181,"title":182,"description":183,"keyLinks":184,"stats":257},"topic","/article/foundations/equations/elementary/","Elementary Equations","\n    Learn how to solve and transform elementary equations step by step.\n    Simple and visual, with clear examples and without memorizing a bunch of obscure rules.\n    This is a key foundational skill in mathematics and the exact sciences.\n  ",[185,193,200,207,214,221,229,236,243,250],{"link":186,"schemaName":187,"title":188,"key":189,"seo":190,"description":192},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/?element=equality","accent_term","Equality",{},{"title":191},"What is equality?","Two expressions with an equals sign \"=\" between them. Equality can be true (2 = 2) or false (2 = 0).",{"link":194,"schemaName":195,"title":196,"key":197,"seo":198,"description":199},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/?element=equality-false-true","diagram","True and false equality",{},{},"If identical objects stand on the sides of the = sign, then the equality is true. If different -- false.",{"link":201,"schemaName":187,"title":202,"key":203,"seo":204,"description":206},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/?element=equation","Equation",{},{"title":205},"What is an equation?","An equality in which there is one or more unknowns or variables.",{"link":208,"schemaName":187,"title":209,"key":210,"seo":211,"description":213},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/?element=equation-solution","Solving an Equation",{},{"title":212},"What does it mean to solve an equation?","\"Solutions\" or \"roots\" of an equation are numbers that, when substituted for unknowns, turn it into a true equality.\n          \"To solve an equation\" means to find all its roots and prove that there are no other roots.",{"link":215,"schemaName":216,"title":217,"key":218,"seo":219,"description":220},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/?element=same-action-rule","accent_statement","Same Action Rule",{},{},"If the same action is performed on both sides of a true equality, the resulting equality will also be true.",{"link":222,"schemaName":223,"title":224,"key":225,"seo":226,"description":228},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/?element=common-mistakes","list","Mistakes when solving equations",{},{"title":227},"Common mistakes when solving equations","A list of common mistakes that beginners make when solving equations.",{"link":230,"schemaName":231,"title":232,"key":233,"seo":234,"description":235},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/?element=why-solve-equations","heading","Why Solve Equations?",{},{},"A set of examples requiring the ability to solve equations to work with.",{"link":237,"schemaName":231,"title":238,"key":239,"seo":240,"description":242},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/?element=the-idiot-s-triangle","Triangle of Formulas",{},{"title":241},"Magic triangle of formulas","A mnemonic technique for memorizing simple formulas.",{"link":244,"schemaName":231,"title":245,"key":246,"seo":247,"description":249},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/?element=equations-in-life","Equations in Life",{},{"title":248},"Where are equations used in life?","A selection of problems and situations from real life that can be solved if translated into equations.",{"link":251,"schemaName":252,"title":253,"key":254,"seo":255,"description":256},"/practice/foundations/equations/elementary/?element=linear-root","problems","Linear equations formula",{},{},"Formula by which you can very quickly find the root of any equation of the form Ax + B = 0.",{"elements":258},{"accent_term":259,"accent_statement":260,"accent_important":151,"problem":261},3,1,36,{"type":177,"link":263,"title":264,"description":265,"stats":266},"/group/foundations/equations/quadratic/","Quadratic Equations","\n    A comprehensive overview of quadratic equations, including quadratic trinomials, completing the square,\n    the discriminant, Vieta’s formulas, factoring, real-life applications, and even methods for solving them mentally.\n  ",{"materials":259,"elements":267},{"accent_term":151,"accent_statement":259,"a